{"_id": "human_resources--hr_policies:_doc--n--62142", "text": "{\n    \"policy_id\": \"IT-SEC-001\",\n    \"policy_title\": \"Acceptable Use of Company Technology\",\n    \"policy_description\": \"A comprehensive guide outlining the acceptable use of all company-owned computers, networks, and software. This includes details on security protocols, data protection, and employee responsibilities regarding technology use.  It covers all aspects of IT security from password management to preventing phishing attacks and data breaches. Regular training is required for all employees. This policy is critical to maintaining the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of company information.  It also addresses the legal and ethical implications of technology misuse.\",\n    \"effective_date\": \"2022-11-01\",\n    \"last_updated\": \"2024-02-15\",\n    \"applicable_departments\": [\n        \"All\"\n    ],\n    \"policy_document_url\": \"https://example.com/it/security-policy\"\n}"}
